  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Transitive ichidan verb. X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{煮|に}つける. Refers specifically to simmering ingredients in a strongly seasoned liquid so that the flavor soaks in.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{魚|さかな}→魚：00499_sakana⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{煮|に}つける: to simmer fish\n- ⟦{甘辛|あまから}く→甘辛い：27507_amakarai⟧{煮|に}つける: to simmer in a sweet-and-salty seasoning\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{煮込|にこ}む→煮込む：05822_nikomu⟧: to stew — long simmering, often for soups and stews; less focus on seasoning soaking in\n- ⟦{煮|に}る→煮る：01971_niru⟧: to boil; to cook — the general term, neutral about seasoning",
